      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(ollama): fall back when native streams end early",
        "body": "Closes #100460.\n\n## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes an issue where a native Ollama chat stream ending before its final response could dead-end a configured model fallback chain.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nThe Ollama plugin now classifies only its exact incomplete-stream error as `server_error` for both local Ollama and Ollama Cloud. The stream producer and provider classifier share one constant, so this vendor-specific rule stays in the provider boundary and unrelated Ollama errors remain unclassified.\n\n## User Impact\n\nUsers with model fallbacks configured can advance to the next candidate when Ollama closes an incomplete native stream instead of receiving a terminal request failure.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Exact head: `2f472a13e1ad508a5759d6b3ab32b71ea12de237`.\n- `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs extensions/ollama/index.test.ts extensions/ollama/src/stream-runtime.test.ts` - 2 files, 163 tests passed.\n- `git diff --check origin/main...HEAD` passed.\n- Exact-head hosted CI run `28762791539` is in progress.\n- Fresh branch AutoReview reported no actionable findings and rated the patch correct with 0.86 confidence.\n- Upstream `ollama/ollama@964ea42` defines `ChatResponse.Done` as the completion signal and emits it from the chat completion response, confirming EOF before that response is incomplete.\n- Proof gap: validation did not force a live Ollama daemon to truncate mid-stream; the producer error and provider classification are covered directly.\n\nAI assistance: Codex performed maintainer review, upstream contract inspection, regression-proof selection, and landing preparation.\n",
        "branch": "fix-ollama-stream-end-fallback-100460",
        "head_sha": "cb6b626c1537697fa97a18c472c76632b58574a1",
        "author": "turbotheturtle",
